WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.916 --> 00:00:04.921
Does everything happen for a reason?

00:00:05.201 --> 00:00:08.402
So I got a great question from one of my Facebook fans

00:00:08.497 --> 00:00:10.509
(love you guys!) Domenic, who wrote in to say

00:00:10.509 --> 00:00:12.705
“Evan, hello! Wishing this finds you well.

00:00:12.919 --> 00:00:15.562
Just curious, what are your thoughts on that famous line

00:00:15.562 --> 00:00:17.080
“Everything happens for a reason.”

00:00:17.177 --> 00:00:19.955
Are you in support of it? I’d appreciate your input when time permits.

00:00:20.132 --> 00:00:21.255
Thanks. -Domenic”

00:00:21.617 --> 00:00:23.181
So thanks for the question Domenic.

00:00:23.543 --> 00:00:24.811
This one…

00:00:25.347 --> 00:00:27.470
this one stressed me out.

00:00:27.887 --> 00:00:29.382
Trying to think of an answer

00:00:29.583 --> 00:00:32.725
and I was walking outside for longer than usual

00:00:32.725 --> 00:00:34.788
trying to think of where I stood on this

00:00:34.974 --> 00:00:39.144
mostly because I don’t think about this a lot.

00:00:39.162 --> 00:00:40.972
You know, if you ask me about raising capital

00:00:40.972 --> 00:00:43.764
or marketing or startups or web or technology

00:00:44.114 --> 00:00:45.952
stuff that I live and breathe every day

00:00:46.032 --> 00:00:48.114
it’s easy for me to come up with answers for you.

00:00:48.393 --> 00:00:51.376
This one is not part of my daily

00:00:52.066 --> 00:00:53.499
Routine.

00:00:53.503 --> 00:00:56.474
You know, I don’t say that line to people and so

00:00:58.536 --> 00:01:00.579
it hurt my brain to think of

00:01:00.579 --> 00:01:02.082
the answer for you.

00:01:02.082 --> 00:01:03.547
But you asked for a video response

00:01:03.547 --> 00:01:04.967
and so

00:01:04.967 --> 00:01:06.387
I’m going to give it to you regardless.

00:01:06.387 --> 00:01:07.808
How do I feel about it?

00:01:07.983 --> 00:01:11.627
What I like about it is the uplifting

00:01:11.627 --> 00:01:12.271
positive

00:01:12.462 --> 00:01:13.483
“believe”

00:01:13.545 --> 00:01:15.304
message in it, right.

00:01:15.326 --> 00:01:15.986
Usually you say

00:01:15.986 --> 00:01:17.039
“Everything happens for a reason”

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:19.865
when something bad happens, right,

00:01:19.865 --> 00:01:21.147
at least that’s my view of it.

00:01:21.275 --> 00:01:23.077
When something really good happens I guess you could say

00:01:23.077 --> 00:01:24.370
“Everything happens for a reason”

00:01:24.394 --> 00:01:26.171
but it’s more when something bad happens;

00:01:26.171 --> 00:01:27.474
when your company goes down

00:01:27.474 --> 00:01:29.288
when your dream gets crushed

00:01:29.452 --> 00:01:31.654
you know, something terrible happens in your life

00:01:31.654 --> 00:01:32.370
or business you say

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:34.203
“Well, everything happens for a reason.”

00:01:34.218 --> 00:01:36.795
And you use it as an encouragement to that person to say

00:01:36.795 --> 00:01:38.290
“Hey, you know, you’re going to bounce back.

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:39.400
Things are going to happen.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.215
Keep the faith, keep believing.” right,

00:01:41.215 --> 00:01:42.620
that’s the uplifting message.

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:44.283
So I love that component to it.

00:01:44.527 --> 00:01:47.643
What I don’t like about it is giving up.

00:01:48.289 --> 00:01:49.379
At least in my view

00:01:49.379 --> 00:01:51.721
giving up the personal accountability

00:01:51.721 --> 00:01:54.063
or responsibility

00:01:54.063 --> 00:01:56.407
like things are just going to happen for you

00:01:56.507 --> 00:01:58.493
without you doing anything, right.

00:01:58.545 --> 00:02:02.015
You want your dream to happen you got to work hard at it.

00:02:02.015 --> 00:02:04.125
You got to put in effort and hours

00:02:04.125 --> 00:02:06.355
and labor and you’re going to go through crap

00:02:06.355 --> 00:02:09.620
to get there and a lot of bad stuff is going to happen to you

00:02:09.627 --> 00:02:10.780
in your life and your business

00:02:10.786 --> 00:02:12.369
to get your company off the ground.

00:02:12.616 --> 00:02:14.442
And you look at famous entrepreneurs

00:02:14.442 --> 00:02:18.451
who went from nothing to creating billion dollar empires

00:02:18.451 --> 00:02:20.381
and they often went through years

00:02:20.381 --> 00:02:22.542
of terrible stuff happening to them

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:26.453
and them seeing zero growth and people telling them to quit

00:02:26.453 --> 00:02:27.993
and somehow they kept going.

00:02:28.395 --> 00:02:31.396
And they did that because they

00:02:31.556 --> 00:02:32.687
they were a little crazy.

00:02:32.767 --> 00:02:35.051
You have to be a little crazy to be an entrepreneur

00:02:35.454 --> 00:02:37.141
and they believed in their idea so much

00:02:37.808 --> 00:02:39.784
and in the potential that they kept going.

00:02:39.786 --> 00:02:42.724
They really had to do this and that’s what helped

00:02:42.724 --> 00:02:44.215
them become super successful

00:02:44.248 --> 00:02:46.828
even though it was all failure at the start.

00:02:47.514 --> 00:02:53.217
And so I liked the uplifting positive vibe to it

00:02:53.217 --> 00:02:55.074
you know; everything happens for a reason

00:02:55.078 --> 00:02:56.707
you’re going to get there.

00:02:56.847 --> 00:03:00.248
But I also think that if you want to become successful

00:03:00.248 --> 00:03:01.433
you got to put in the work

00:03:01.433 --> 00:03:02.995
you got to really love what you’re doing

00:03:03.014 --> 00:03:05.257
you got to be really committed to this project

00:03:05.257 --> 00:03:07.644
and that’s what’s going to help you take off.

00:03:07.751 --> 00:03:09.533
So I don’t know if that answers your question

00:03:09.533 --> 00:03:11.430
but I promised you a video response

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:13.172
and so here it is.

00:03:13.172 --> 00:03:14.550
But at the end of the day, honestly,

00:03:14.653 --> 00:03:17.099
I don’t have a super strong opinion on it.

00:03:17.207 --> 00:03:18.294
It’s not a part of my

00:03:18.447 --> 00:03:21.200
day to day vocabulary or thought process.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.761
And so, anyway,

00:03:23.761 --> 00:03:24.894
those are my thoughts.

00:03:25.344 --> 00:03:26.517
If you guys like this video

00:03:26.707 --> 00:03:27.921
you can support me

00:03:27.921 --> 00:03:29.434
by clicking on the link in the description.

00:03:29.749 --> 00:03:31.152
Leave a comment

00:03:31.152 --> 00:03:32.875
and let me know what your thoughts are

00:03:32.875 --> 00:03:34.600
on that famous line

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:36.756
and maybe that’ll create some interesting discussion

00:03:37.395 --> 00:03:38.897
on YouTube and I look forward to

00:03:38.897 --> 00:03:39.959
hearing what you guys have to say.

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:40.975
And click on my face,

00:03:41.025 --> 00:03:41.884
subscribe to the channel.

00:03:42.234 --> 00:03:44.164
Thank you so much, I’ll see you soon.

